IMPORT prelude

-- Debt Collection Act 2022 (Singapore) -- who needs a licence or a class licence to collect debts (ss 2, 6, First Schedule), who
-- may act as an individual debt collector (ss 17, 18), what the offences carry and which are arrestable (ss 6(5), 7(6), 17(3),
-- 18(2), 33), failing an officer's requirement (s 34(1), (4), (5)), composition (s 35), convictions that ground cancellation of a
-- collector's approval (s 25(1)(d), Second Schedule), appeals (s 37) and the transitional period (s 46).
--
-- Edition: informal consolidation, "version in force from 1/12/2023", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/DCA2022.txt (Act 27 of 2022; SSO page retrieved 2026-10-01, "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026").
-- The latest amendment annotated in the text is S 723/2023 wef 01/12/2023 (accountants added to the excluded persons; new Second
-- Schedule entries).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for everyday-life relevance: anyone in Singapore who owes money and is chased by an agency, a bank, a card
-- issuer or a moneylender meets this Act, as does anyone who takes a job as a debt collector. (An automated count found 1 of the
-- 527 deposited Singapore Acts citing it by title; that count undercounts and is not a measure of importance.)
-- SCOPED to the provisions above. Not encoded: licence applications and conditions (ss 7-13 except 7(6)), class licence orders
-- (ss 14-15), codes of practice (s 16) beyond NOTES, approval procedure and conditions (ss 19-21), regulatory action against
-- licensees and its procedure (ss 22-24, 26-28) except the s 25(1)(d) conviction grounds, enforcement powers (ss 29-32),
-- corporate and partnership liability (ss 39-40), service (s 42), and the regulation-making power (s 45), which is where any
-- rules on how collectors may behave towards debtors would sit.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows (the skill itself
-- was not available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Debt Collection Act 2022 -- collecting debts`

-- s 2(1): "debt collection business" means the business carried on by a person of collecting any debt from a debtor "(a) on behalf
-- of another person; or (b) where the firstmentioned person has acquired the debt".
-- First Schedule Part 1 (excluded persons) includes, "when acting in that capacity", licensed insolvency practitioners and
-- regulated legal practitioners; Singapore law practices; (ed) chartered accountants acting as such [S 723/2023]; (f) a person who
-- acquires debts "through acquiring or merging with a business (other than a debt collection business)"; (g) a person who acquires
-- debts "through the seizure of accounts receivable under a security agreement".
-- First Schedule Part 2 (regulated businesses): banks, merchant banks, licensed credit or charge card issuers, finance companies,
-- licensed or exempt moneylenders.
DECLARE Collector IS ONE OF
    `a debt collection agency collecting for a client`
    `a company that bought the debt from the creditor`
    `a bank collecting its own loan`
    `a credit card issuer collecting its own card debt`
    `a licensed moneylender collecting its own loan`
    `a landlord collecting its own rent`
    `a law practice collecting for a client`
    `a licensed insolvency practitioner acting as such`
    `a chartered accountant acting as such`
    `a company that took over receivables in a merger`
    `a secured lender that seized receivables`

§§ `2 and First Schedule -- who is caught`

-- Inference: the excluded persons in paragraph 1(a)-(e) and (f), (g) are treated here as persons who would otherwise be carrying
-- on a debt collection business; the Act excludes them without saying so.
GIVEN `the collector` IS A Collector
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an excluded person` IF
    CONSIDER `the collector`
    WHEN `a law practice collecting for a client` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licensed insolvency practitioner acting as such` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a chartered accountant acting as such` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a company that took over receivables in a merger` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a secured lender that seized receivables` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the collector` IS A Collector
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carries on a debt collection business` IF
    CONSIDER `the collector`
    WHEN `a debt collection agency collecting for a client` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a company that bought the debt from the creditor` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `is an excluded person` `the collector`

-- s 6(2) and First Schedule Part 2: the person "carries on a regulated business" and collects a debt "owed to the person in the
-- course of the regulated business".
GIVEN `the collector` IS A Collector
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a regulated business collecting its own debt` IF
    CONSIDER `the collector`
    WHEN `a bank collecting its own loan` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a credit card issuer collecting its own card debt` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licensed moneylender collecting its own loan` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 6(1), (4): a licence is needed to carry on a debt collection business; "Subsections (1) and (3) do not apply to an excluded
-- person".
GIVEN `the collector` IS A Collector
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `needs a licence` IF
    `carries on a debt collection business` `the collector` AND (NOT `is an excluded person` `the collector`)

-- s 6(2): a regulated business needs a class licence. The s 6(4) exclusion does not reach subsection (2).
GIVEN `the collector` IS A Collector
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `needs a class licence` IF
    `is a regulated business collecting its own debt` `the collector`

-- A creditor that is neither in a debt collection business nor a regulated business collecting its own debt is outside s 6.
GIVEN `the collector` IS A Collector
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is outside section 6` IF
    (NOT `needs a licence` `the collector`) AND (NOT `needs a class licence` `the collector`) AND (NOT `is an excluded person` `the collector`)

§§ `6 and 46 -- operating without a licence`

-- s 6(1): a person must not, on or after the start date, carry on a debt collection business "unless the person is an ENTITY which
-- is authorised to carry on the debt collection business by a valid licence". s 2(1) "entity": a registered company, a sole
-- proprietorship or partnership registered under the Business Names Registration Act 2014, an LLP, an LP, or a prescribed structure.
-- s 2(4)(a): a licensee is not regarded as licensed while its licence is suspended under s 22(2)(b) or 24(2).
-- s 6(6): "start date" means the date 3 months after commencement of s 6.
-- s 46(1), (2): a person carrying on the business immediately before the start date who applied for a licence before that date,
-- and whose application was not granted, refused or withdrawn before that date, may continue until the licence is granted or the
-- application is finally refused or withdrawn.
GIVEN `was carrying on the business before the start date` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `applied for a licence before the start date` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `application decided or withdrawn before the start date` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `application since finally refused or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may continue under section 46` IF
        `was carrying on the business before the start date`
    AND `applied for a licence before the start date`
    AND (NOT `application decided or withdrawn before the start date`)
    AND (NOT `application since finally refused or withdrawn`)

GIVEN `the collector` IS A Collector,
      `on or after the start date` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds a valid licence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `licence is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `covered by a class licence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `protected by section 46` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `collecting is an offence under section 6` IF
        `on or after the start date`
    AND (    (    `needs a licence` `the collector`
              AND (NOT (`is an entity` AND `holds a valid licence` AND (NOT `licence is suspended`)))
              AND (NOT `protected by section 46`))
         OR  (`needs a class licence` `the collector` AND (NOT `covered by a class licence`)))

-- s 6(5): (a) a fine not exceeding $20,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years or both; but (b) for a repeat offender "a fine of
-- not less than $20,000 and not more than $100,000" or imprisonment not exceeding 5 years or both. "Repeat offender" is not
-- defined anywhere in the deposited text of this Act.
GIVEN `repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 6` MEANS
    IF `repeat offender` THEN 100000 ELSE 20000

GIVEN `repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum fine under section 6` MEANS
    IF `repeat offender` THEN 20000 ELSE 0

GIVEN `repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months under section 6` MEANS
    IF `repeat offender` THEN 60 ELSE 24

§§ `17 and 46(3), (4) -- individuals acting as debt collectors`

-- s 17(1): an individual must not act as a debt collector for a person who carries on a debt collection business unless "(a) the
-- person is a licensee which is approved to deploy the individual ... under section 20; or (b) the person is the individual's
-- EMPLOYER and is an excluded person".
-- s 17(2): for a person who carries on a regulated business, only if "(a) the person is the individual's employer and is a class
-- licensee; and (b)" the debt is one the person is authorised to collect under an applicable class licence.
-- s 2(4)(c): an approval is not regarded as granted while suspended under s 25(2)(c) or 27(2).
-- s 46(3), (4): an individual deployed immediately before the s 17 start date by a principal who applied for a licence in time may
-- continue to be deployed for the period there stated. Collapsed here into one flag.
GIVEN `the principal` IS A Collector,
      `on or after the start date` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the principal is the individual's employer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the principal is a licensee approved to deploy the individual` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the principal is a class licensee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the debt is within the class licence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `protected by section 46` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `acting as a debt collector is an offence` IF
        `on or after the start date`
    AND (NOT `protected by section 46`)
    AND (    (    `carries on a debt collection business` `the principal`
              AND (NOT `the principal is a licensee approved to deploy the individual`)
              AND (NOT (`the principal is the individual's employer` AND `is an excluded person` `the principal`)))
         OR  (    `is a regulated business collecting its own debt` `the principal`
              AND (NOT (`the principal is the individual's employer` AND `the principal is a class licensee` AND `the debt is within the class licence`))))

§§ `6(5), 7(6), 17(3), 18(2), 28(3), 33 -- the offences compared`

-- s 6(5): $20,000 / 2 years (repeat: $100,000 / 5 years). s 7(6): a knowingly false statement in a licence application, $10,000 / 2
-- years. s 17(3): $10,000 / 12 months (repeat: $20,000 / 2 years). s 18(2): a licensee deploying an unapproved individual, the same.
-- s 28(3): failing to notify the cessation of a deployment, $10,000 / 2 years.
-- s 33: "Every offence under the following provisions is arrestable ... (a) section 6(5) in respect of a contravention of
-- section 6(1); (b) section 17(3)."
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `running an unlicensed debt collection business`
    `a regulated business collecting without a class licence`
    `holding out as a debt collection business without a licence`
    `acting as an unapproved debt collector`
    `a licensee deploying an unapproved debt collector`
    `a knowingly false statement in a licence application`
    `failing to notify that a collector has stopped`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is arrestable` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `running an unlicensed debt collection business` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acting as an unapproved debt collector` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for a first offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `running an unlicensed debt collection business` THEN 20000
    WHEN `a regulated business collecting without a class licence` THEN 20000
    WHEN `holding out as a debt collection business without a licence` THEN 20000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months for a first offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `acting as an unapproved debt collector` THEN 12
    WHEN `a licensee deploying an unapproved debt collector` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 24

§§ `34 -- failing to do what an officer requires`

-- s 34(1): a person who "without reasonable excuse" fails to do anything required by an inspecting or compliance officer under
-- s 30(1) or 31(1)(a), (b) or a s 31(1)(c) notice -- fine not exceeding $10,000.
-- (4): a defence "to prove, on a balance of probabilities," that the person (a) does not possess the document, information or
-- article, or (b) took all reasonable steps to obtain it and could not.
-- (5): "it is a reasonable excuse" to refuse "if doing so might tend to incriminate that person".
GIVEN `was required by an officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `complied` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `compliance might incriminate them` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had another reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved they did not possess it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved they took all reasonable steps to obtain it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing the requirement is an offence` IF
        `was required by an officer`
    AND (NOT `complied`)
    AND (NOT `compliance might incriminate them`)
    AND (NOT `had another reasonable excuse`)
    AND (NOT `proved they did not possess it`)
    AND (NOT `proved they took all reasonable steps to obtain it`)

§§ `35 -- composition`

-- s 35(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount
-- of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence"; (b) $5,000.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a composition can be` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

§§ `25(1)(d) and Second Schedule -- convictions that ground cancelling a collector's approval`

-- s 25(1)(d): the Licensing Officer may cancel an individual's approval if the individual has "(during the period of approval)"
-- been convicted of (i) an offence under this Act; (ii) an offence, in Singapore or elsewhere, involving dishonesty; (iii) an
-- offence in the Second Schedule; or (iv) detained under the Criminal Law (Temporary Provisions) Act 1955 or the Internal Security
-- Act 1960. Second Schedule item 6: offences under ss 3-7 of the Protection from Harassment Act 2014; item 8: s 3 of the Vandalism
-- Act 1966; item 4: ss 19, 47, 49 of the Moneylenders Act 2008; item 3A: s 11(1)(a) of the Miscellaneous Offences (Public Order
-- and Nuisance) Act 1906 [S 723/2023]. Other grounds (unfit, s 25(1)(b)) are not modelled.
DECLARE Conviction IS ONE OF
    `an offence under this Act`
    `a dishonesty offence committed abroad`
    `harassment under the Protection from Harassment Act`
    `vandalism under the Vandalism Act`
    `an offence under section 47 of the Moneylenders Act`
    `a speeding offence`

GIVEN `the conviction` IS A Conviction, `during the period of approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conviction is a ground to cancel the approval` IF
    `during the period of approval` AND
    (CONSIDER `the conviction`
     WHEN `a speeding offence` THEN FALSE
     OTHERWISE TRUE)

§§ `37 -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 37(2): an appeal "must be made within 14 days after the date the decision appealed against is served"; (5) the Minister's
-- decision "is final"; (7) an appeal "does not affect the operation of the decision", which must be complied with pending the
-- appeal "unless otherwise directed by the Minister".
GIVEN `days after service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `days after service` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `the Minister directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision must be obeyed pending the appeal` IF
    NOT `the Minister directed otherwise`
